speechtext:
Contract TOX80-1695/2 was awarded by the Department of Supply and Services on behalf of the Department of National Defence to J.l. DeNure (Chatham) Ltd. for the rental of school buses. The contract was awarded on June 13, 1980, and was valued at $23,400.
(a)	A total of ten buses were involved; five buses for the period June 16 to August 22, 1980, and five for the period July 2 to August 22, 1980;
(b)	The buses were used to transport approximately 1,800 cadets attending the Ipperwash summer camp in June, July and August, 1980.

Contract QUE80-1938/1 was awarded by the Department of Supply and Services on behalf of the Department of National Defence to Location d'autos et camions, Budget de Chicoutimi for the rental of cars and mini-buses. The contract was awarded on June 13, 1980, and was valued at $12,000.
(a)	Seven cars and three mini-buses;
(b)	The vehicles, in (a) above, were used to transport approximately 1,800 cadets to summer camps in Bagotville, Jonquiere and St. Honore, Quebec during the months of June, July and August, 1980.

I wish I had been given notice of that question to be able to answer it properly.
[English}
The fact is that for a long time the hon. member for Qu'Appelle-Moose Mountain (Mr. Hamilton) has been pressing the government to correct the Family Allowances Act with respect to family allowances and orphans. Unfortunately, I am not in a position today to give him any good news, but I can assure him that I fully support future improvements to the system, which I am sure will come.
